---
import PageLayout from "~/layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "~/lib/url";
---
<PageLayout
  eyebrow="Colophon"
  title="About this website"
  lede="How this site is built and where the content lives."
>
  <div class="prose max-w-3xl">
    <p>
      This site is built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> and
      <a href="https://tailwindcss.com">Tailwind CSS</a>, deployed via GitHub Pages.
      The people, projects, publications and news are a knowledge graph: YAML files under
      <code>kg/</code>, described by a <a href="https://linkml.io">LinkML</a> schema and
      compiled to RDF when the site builds. The pages are generated from that graph, which
      you can download as <a href={withBase("/kg/sensein.ttl")}>Turtle</a> or
      <a href={withBase("/kg/sensein.jsonld")}>JSON-LD</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Where to edit content</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>People — <code>kg/people.yaml</code>, and their roles in <code>kg/memberships.yaml</code></li>
      <li>Projects — <code>kg/projects.yaml</code>, funding in <code>kg/grants.yaml</code></li>
      <li>Publications — <code>kg/publications.yaml</code></li>
      <li>Images and figures — <code>kg/images.yaml</code></li>
      <li>News — <code>kg/news.yaml</code></li>
      <li>Collaborators — <code>kg/collaborations.yaml</code></li>
      <li>Blog posts — <code>src/content/posts/*.md</code></li>
      <li>Page copy — <code>src/pages/*.astro</code></li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Previewing changes</h2>
    <p>
      Every pull request gets an isolated preview at
      <code>sensein.group/pr-preview/pr-N/</code> automatically — open a PR and watch the
      checks for the link.
    </p>
    <h2>Lineage</h2>
    <p>
      The earlier version of this site was adapted from the
      <a href="https://github.com/mpa139/allanlab">Allan Lab</a> Jekyll template (MIT
      licensed). This rewrite preserves the YAML-driven approach.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
